" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T13:19:25-08:00","id":1526772,"title":"","content":"Accurate answer - <b>Assassins</b> is like 'sorta alternative' setting to <b>TC Core</b>, like <b>Phobe Trust</b> book is one, on official timeline image below. They are both 'optional canon' - that means main gameline material are omitting those, but you SG can decide they are canon for your game. I'm huge <b>Assassins</b> book fan, so in my games, <b>Assassins </b>stuff is canon and <b>Aberrant</b> is not ( or, rather, <b>Aberrant</b> is moved in to 2040s in my timeline as N-Day is only slowly approaching in year 2030 )<br /> <br /> For my alternative Trinity 'fancanon' using Assassins - <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468693-tc-assasins-instead-aberrant-on-timeline?p=1498622#post1498622\">see this post and topic</a>. \ud83d\ude09<br /> <img width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/rTrh228.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/rTrh228.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/rTrh228.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T14:30:32-08:00","id":1526776,"title":"","content":"Note that every book is \u201coptional canon\u201d: no Storyguide is <i>ever </i>forced to use any material that he doesn't want to. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bAn important point to consider here is that the TC core setting itself doesn't \u201cfit in\u201d with <b>TC: Aberrant</b>. The latter is set in 2028, ten years after N-Day. By my reckoning, that puts 2023 exactly halfway between N-Day and the \u201cday zero\u201d of the Nova Age. <br /> <br /> The TC core setting doesn't take place between <b>Adventure</b> and <b>Aberrant</b>. It takes place \u201coff to the side\u201d, in an alternate 2020s. <b>Assassins</b> is an official setting for the Trinity Continuum that's set concurrently with the core book's setting: it's exactly as \u201coptional\u201d as the core setting itself is. <br /> <br /> And the same way that Talents can be used in any era, so can Assassins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reaction